  human-intervention-logs/com.azure:azure-core-http-jdk-httpclient:1.1.4/add-new-library-support/pi-generation-2026-09-18T00-51-21-022093Z.log:17314:  | **Repository automation (Forge)** | Generate or repair metadata using LLM-driven pipelines. | Per coordinate, the toolkit can: (1) **add support for a new library** — generate a JUnit / Kotlin / Scala test suite, scaffold metadata, and iterate until JVM-mode tests pass and dynamic-access is collected ([`add_new_library_support.py`](../../forge/ai_workflows/drivers/add_new_library_support.py)); (2) **fix a Java compilation (`javac`) failure** raised by a library version bump ([`fix_javac_fail.py`](../../forge/ai_workflows/drivers/fix_javac_fail.py)); (3) **fix a JVM-mode (`javaTest`) runtime failure** raised by a version bump ([`fix_java_run_fail.py`](../../forge/ai_workflows/drivers/fix_java_run_fail.py)); (4) **fix a `native-image` runtime failure** raised by a version bump ([`fix_ni_run.py`](../../forge/ai_workflows/drivers/fix_ni_run.py)); (5) **improve dynamic-access coverage** of already-supported libraries by targeting uncovered call sites; (6) **post-generation repair** of the metadata produced by a previous run ([`post_generation_fix.py`](../../forge/ai_workflows/core/post_generation_fix.py), [`metadata_fix.py`](../../forge/ai_workflows/core/metadata_fix.py)). Each task runs Gradle tasks against a worktree of this repo, appends a schema-validated metrics record, and — when invoked through [`forge/git_scripts/publish_*.py`](../../forge/git_scripts/) — pushes a verified branch that trusted GitHub Actions turn into a PR for human review. See [forge/docs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md](../../forge/docs/functional-spec/functional-spec.md). |
  human-intervention-logs/com.azure:azure-core-http-jdk-httpclient:1.1.4/add-new-library-support/pi-generation-2026-09-18T00-51-21-022093Z.log:17366:  Every Monday the `create-scheduled-release` workflow packages metadata into the next numbered release if it has changed (§AR-create-scheduled-release). The release is deliberately not gated on the periodic `test-all-metadata` sweep: merged metadata is already gated per-PR (§5.3), and the sweep exercises bleeding-edge JDK and native-image configurations whose failures must not stall the release cadence. Numbered releases consider only semantic version tags when computing the previous version tag, so floating snapshot tags such as `SNAPSHOT` cannot affect the permanent release cadence.
  human-intervention-logs/com.azure:azure-core-http-jdk-httpclient:1.1.4/add-new-library-support/pi-generation-2026-09-18T00-51-21-022093Z.log:17410:  | `fails-javac-compile` | Issue | New-version compatibility failed during the `compileTestJava` / Java compilation stage. |
  human-intervention-logs/com.azure:azure-core-http-jdk-httpclient:1.1.4/add-new-library-support/pi-generation-2026-09-18T00-51-21-022093Z.log:17411:  | `fails-java-run` | Issue | New-version compatibility failed during the `javaTest` / JVM runtime stage. |
  human-intervention-logs/com.azure:azure-core-http-jdk-httpclient:1.1.4/add-new-library-support/pi-generation-2026-09-18T00-51-21-022093Z.log:17412:  | `fails-native-image-build` | Issue | New-version compatibility failed while building the native image. These issues are assigned for maintainer follow-up. |
  human-intervention-logs/com.azure:azure-core-http-jdk-httpclient:1.1.4/add-new-library-support/pi-generation-2026-09-18T00-51-21-022093Z.log:17413:  | `fails-native-image-run` | Issue | New-version compatibility failed while running the native image. |
  human-intervention-logs/com.azure:azure-core-http-jdk-httpclient:1.1.4/add-new-library-support/pi-generation-2026-09-18T00-51-21-022093Z.log:17423:  | `high-priority` | Issue | Highest work-queue urgency marker. Compatibility automation adds it to failed updates for artifacts whose latest index entry sets `high-priority: true`, and Forge processes it before `priority` and regular issues in the same pipeline batch. |
  human-intervention-logs/com.azure:azure-core-http-jdk-httpclient:1.1.4/add-new-library-support/pi-generation-2026-09-18T00-51-21-022093Z.log:17425:  | `human-intervention` | Issue / PR | Automation could not safely complete the work without manual follow-up, or automated PR review requested changes. |
  human-intervention-logs/com.azure:azure-core-http-jdk-httpclient:1.1.4/add-new-library-support/pi-generation-2026-09-18T00-51-21-022093Z.log:17472:  **2. `<groupId>/<artifactId>/index.json`** — one per supported artifact, schema [metadata-library-index-schema-v2.3.0.json](../../metadata/schemas/metadata-library-index-schema-v2.3.0.json). It is a JSON **array** of entries. Metadata entries require `metadata-version`, `tested-versions`, and `allowed-packages`, with optional `default-for` (Java regex), `latest: true`, `override: true`, `requires: ["<group>:<artifact>", …]`, `test-version`, `skipped-versions`, `language`, `auto-update: true`, `high-priority: true`, and the four URL fields. `auto-update` is a repository-automation opt-in allowed only on the unique `latest: true` entry; omission disables automated upstream-version compatibility checks for the artifact. `high-priority` is likewise allowed only on that entry and makes failed compatibility updates highest-priority Forge work. Plugin-relevant fields are the first six.
  human-intervention-logs/com.azure:azure-core-http-jdk-httpclient:1.1.4/add-new-library-support/pi-generation-2026-09-18T00-51-21-022093Z.log:17540:  - **Compatibility budget.** `verify-new-library-version-compatibility` caps each scheduled run at a fixed library budget and at most 30 newer versions per library, expanding across the configured GraalVM JDK/OS combinations, and creates one aggregated GitHub issue per failed `(library, version)` pair.
  human-intervention-logs/com.azure:azure-core-http-jdk-httpclient:1.1.4/add-new-library-support/pi-generation-2026-09-18T00-51-21-022093Z.log:17542:  - **Full sweep.** `test-all-metadata` runs only on a weekly Sunday schedule or manual dispatch in the main repository, uses 85 batches, isolates failed batches down to concrete library versions, publishes result and failure-log artifacts, and fails affected matrix batches. It surfaces sweep regressions but does not gate the scheduled release (§4.4).
