 job failed during test generation/exploration for `com.azure:azure-core-http-jdk-httpclient:1.1.4`.\n\nPreserved work: https://github.com/oracle/graalvm-reachability-metadata/tree/ai%2Fcugurm%2Fhuman-intervention%2Fissue-10052-library-new-request-com.azure-azure-core-http-jdk-httpclient-1.1.4-61d5a329\n\nThe most likely blocker is dynamic-access reporting. Repeated `generateDynamicAccessCoverageReport` runs failed because `nativeTestCompile/dynamic-access` was not produced, so coverage could not be distinguished from genuinely having no dynamic access. The continuation marker remains at exploration iteration 7 with publication pending and no publication metrics. Later recovery did make all 7 generated native tests pass, and metadata, style, and statistics checks succeeded, so final validation itself was not the failure.\n\nPlease inspect:\n\n- `logs/com.azure:azure-core-http-jdk-httpclient:1.1.4/gradle/generateDynamicAccessCoverageReport-2026-09-18T01-25-40-462258Z.log`\n- `logs/com.azure:azure-core-http-jdk-httpclient:1.1.4/gradle-test/gradle-test-2026-09-18T01-35-51-213886Z.log`\n- `logs/com.azure:azure-core-http-jdk-httpclient:1.1.4/gradle-test/gradle-test-2026-09-18T01-44-03-439994Z.log`\n- `logs/com.azure:azure-core-http-jdk-httpclient:1.1.4/metadata-fix/pi.log`\n\nManual next steps:\n\n1. Determine why Native Image tracking produces no dynamic-access output and establish whether the library truly has no dynamic access.\n2. Review and preferably remove the generated `--initialize-at-build-time` workaround in `build.gradle`, replacing it with a solution that does not mask Native Image behavior.\n3. Rerun the coordinate tests and dynamic-access report on all required lanes, then regenerate trustworthy coverage and execution metrics before publication.", "textSignature": "{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_00f2462f1a7d08b2016aac987b3ac087d2b957be502a3d16e5\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}], "api": "openai-codex-responses", "provider": "openai-codex", "model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "u